      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks — and a sweeping HttpServletResponse → org.apache.http.HttpStatus replacement is part of this topic: see \"Use HttpStatus constants outside servlet code\" in the relation chain [change 595601], which does exactly that wherever the dependency is acceptable.\n\nThe topic\u0027s goal is broader than status codes, though — it reduces the whole servlet-API surface Gerrit exposes:\n* Move servlet RawInput adapter to RestApiServlet\n* Remove servlet request from extended audit event\n* Remove servlet-typed RestReadView apply\n* Restrict servlet API Bazel visibility\n* diverse deprecations\n* javadoc cleanups.\n\nA status-code-only replacement wouldn\u0027t cover those.\n\nThe one place I deliberately kept a local int rather than org.apache.http.HttpStatus is this change, because Response is in gerrit-extension-api (the public plugin API) and shouldn\u0027t gain an Apache HttpComponents dep for a private check (details in the inline comment).",
      "parentUuid": "961cce9c_fa24a25c",
      "revId": "004d7548948fd3972a98309b867155ddd8d833d6",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
