      "writtenOn": "2026-06-28T06:05:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good idea in general, but I\u0027d keep the local int here — and the reasoning is now in the commit message.\n\nThis file is in gerrit-extension-api (the published plugin API), and the constant is only a private, internal bound check in withStatusCode() (statusCode \u003c 500), not something plugins consume. Importing org.apache.http.HttpStatus would pull Apache HttpComponents (httpcore) into the API jar\u0027s deps — and onto every plugin that compiles against it — just to spell an internal 500, which is the opposite of what this series is doing on the extensions surface.\n\nI did try a Gerrit-owned HttpStatusCode constants class (so plugins get flavour-neutral codes without servlet or HttpClient): [change 591183]. Abandoned for now, as the feedback there also leaned toward HttpClient. Happy to revive it if the project wants a shared source — but pulling HttpComponents in for one private check seems disproportionate.",
